# Bug Verification — <%= projectName %>

_Generated by arbiter. The closing step: prove the fix works, prove it stays fixed,
and prove nothing else broke. A bug is not closed until this checklist is green._

> Evidence trail: the `debug-state-on-failure` hook records failed gate/test runs
> to `.evidence/<task>/DEBUG_STATE.md`. Reference that file here — the transition
> from FAIL entries to a passing run is the durable proof the fix landed.

## 1. Regression Test First

- [ ] A test that **fails on the buggy code** was written (TDD red) and committed
- [ ] The same test **passes on the fixed code** (TDD green)
- [ ] Test path: `_…_`

Without a test that failed before the fix, you have not verified the fix — you
have asserted it.

## 2. Fix Verified

- [ ] Original reproduction steps no longer trigger the bug
- [ ] The root cause from `bug-analysis.md` is addressed (not just the symptom)
- [ ] Blast-radius siblings (other paths sharing the cause) checked

## 3. No Regression

- [ ] Full gate green: `node scripts/check-all.mjs L2`
- [ ] Coverage did not drop below the threshold for the touched files
- [ ] `.evidence/<task>/DEBUG_STATE.md` shows the final command passing

## 4. Evidence

| Artifact | Location |
| -------- | -------- |
| Failing-then-passing test | _path_ |
| Gate run output | _paste / link_ |
| DEBUG_STATE history | `.evidence/<task>/DEBUG_STATE.md` |

## 5. Close-Out

- [ ] Root cause and fix summarised in the PR / issue
- [ ] Follow-up tech debt (if any symptom-only mitigation remained) recorded with a task ID
